le states that\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}c\\times f(t)\\,\\text{d}t=c\\times {\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\n \n\nApplying the cross-product rule, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}c\\times f(t)\\,\\text{d}t & =c\\times {\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =(i+j-k)\\times (4\\,i+2\\,k) \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 1 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 4 & 0 & 2\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{aligned}|i-|\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ 4 & 2\\end{aligned}|j+|\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ 4 & 0\\end{aligned}|k \\\\  & =(2-0)i-(2+4)j+(0-4)k \\\\  & =2i-6j-4k.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14057355/state.json" "file_sha256" "bd85708dc06aa312de092dc6485b222955dc1688ed91ada4549eda4c56dd9f12" "basis" 1850 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14057355/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-32522" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14057355/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "8b7121365a5651064a63e6ad7ea3d7b613dcf9341122c72f075f95529beee1ea" "basis" 1850 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14057355/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-32522" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14057355/state.json" "file_sha256" "bd85708dc06aa312de092dc6485b222955dc1688ed91ada4549eda4c56dd9f12" "basis" 1850 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14057355/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-32522" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "-2i-2j+4k"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14057355/state.json" "file_sha256" "bd85708dc06aa312de092dc6485b222955dc1688ed91ada4549eda4c56dd9f12" "basis" 1850 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14057355/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-32522" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "2i+2j-4k"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14057355/state.json" "file_sha256" "bd85708dc06aa312de092dc6485b222955dc1688ed91ada4549eda4c56dd9f12" "basis" 1850 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14057355/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-32522" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "2i-6j-4k"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14057355/state.json" "file_sha256" "bd85708dc06aa312de092dc6485b222955dc1688ed91ada4549eda4c56dd9f12" "basis" 1850 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14057355/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-32522" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "4i-6j+2k"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14057355/state.json" "file_sha256" "bd85708dc06aa312de092dc6485b222955dc1688ed91ada4549eda4c56dd9f12" "basis" 1850 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14057355/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-32522" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "i+6j+2k"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14057355/state.json" "file_sha256" "bd85708dc06aa312de092dc6485b222955dc1688ed91ada4549eda4c56dd9f12" "basis" 1850 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14057355/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "e-3019" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Calculate $\\displaystyle{\\int_0^2} [  3 \\mathbf f(t)+\\mathbf g(t) ] \\,\\textrm{d}t$ given that $\\displaystyle{\\int_0^2} \\mathbf f(t)\\,\\textrm{d}t=\\left\\langle 16, \\: 2,\\: -2\\right\\rangle$ and $\\displaystyle{\\int_0^2}\\mathbf g(t)\\,\\textrm{d}t=\\left\\langle 2,-4,2\\right\\rangle .$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14057355/example-3019.json" "file_sha256" "b4325214312d2fe2a72d3d0a7c6ae0ef7fc9e2f2ffbf86b7e22b0d47f8fd7959" "basis" 1850 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14057355/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "e-3019" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "From the vector addition and scalar multiplication rules, we have\n\n$$\n\\displaystyle {\\int_0^2 } \\big[ \\, 3 \\mathbf f(t)+\\mathbf g(t) \\, \\big] \\, \\textrm d t =  \\displaystyle {3\\int_0^2 } \\mathbf f(t) \\, \\textrm d t + \\displaystyle {\\int_0^2 } \\mathbf g(t) \\, \\textrm d t.\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{2}[3f(t)+g(t)]\\,\\text{d}t & =3{\\int }_{0}^{2}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t+{\\int }_{0}^{2}g(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =3⟨16,\\,2,\\,-2⟩+⟨2,\\,-4,\\,2⟩ \\\\  & =⟨48,\\,6,\\,-6⟩+⟨2,\\,-4,\\,2⟩ \\\\  & =⟨50,2,-4⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14057355/example-3019.json" "file_sha256" "b4325214312d2fe2a72d3d0a7c6ae0ef7fc9e2f2ffbf86b7e22b0d47f8fd7959" "basis" 1850 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14057355/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "e-8688" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Calculate \n$\\displaystyle\\int_0^2\\mathbf f(t) + \\langle 1,\\:-1,\\:1\\rangle\\,\\textrm{d}t$\ngiven that\n$\\displaystyle\\int_2^0\\mathbf f(t) \\,\\textrm{d}t= \\left\\langle -3, \\: 2, \\: 1 \\right\\rangle.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14057355/example-8688.json" "file_sha256" "5d5fa9256f5c11d4a41de07d95a1c885d0d8124bd806e95348707baa917c3ee8" "basis" 1850 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14057355/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "e-8688" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Let's reverse the limits of integration on the known result:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{2}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t & =-{\\int }_{2}^{0}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =-⟨-3,\\,2,\\,1⟩ \\\\  & =⟨3,\\,-2,\\,-1⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, applying the vector addition rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{2}f(t)+⟨1,\\,-1,\\,1⟩\\,\\text{d}t & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t+{\\int }_{0}^{2}⟨1,\\,-1,\\,1⟩\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =⟨3,\\,-2,\\,-1⟩+⟨t,\\,-t,\\,t⟩{|}_{0}^{2} \\\\  & =⟨3,\\,-2,\\,-1⟩+⟨2,\\,-2,\\,2⟩\\text{ } \\\\  & =⟨5,\\,-4,\\,1⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14057355/example-8688.json" "file_sha256" "5d5fa9256f5c11d4a41de07d95a1c885d0d8124bd806e95348707baa917c3ee8" "basis" 1850 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14057355/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "e-3020" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Calculate \n$\\displaystyle\\int_{-1}^0\\mathbf f(t)\\,\\textrm{d}t$\ngiven that\n$\\displaystyle\\int_0^1\\mathbf f(t)\\,\\textrm{d}t= \\left\\langle \\dfrac{3}{2}, \\: 1, \\: 3 \\right\\rangle$\nand\n$\\displaystyle\\int_{-1}^1\\mathbf f(t)\\,\\textrm{d}t=\\left\\langle 0, \\: 2, \\: 6 \\right\\rangle.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14057355/example-3020.json" "file_sha256" "203f27b71cbdb193ed73d4978a08ef8e94342401b0256735cf0a638d2578da86" "basis" 1850 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14057355/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "e-3020" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Using the adjacent intervals, we get\n\n$$\n\\int_{-1}^1\\mathbf f(t)\\,\\textrm{d}t=\\int_{-1}^0\\mathbf f(t)\\,\\textrm{d}t+\\int_0^1\\mathbf f(t)\\,\\textrm{d}t .\n$$\n\nWe can rearrange the above as follows:\n\n$$\n\\int_{-1}^0\\mathbf f(t)\\,\\textrm{d}t = \n\\int_{-1}^1\\mathbf f(t)\\,\\textrm{d}t - \\int_0^1\\mathbf f(t)\\,\\textrm{d}t\n$$\n\nFinally, using the given information, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-1}^{0}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t & ={\\int }_{-1}^{1}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t-{\\int }_{0}^{1}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =⟨0,\\,2,\\,6⟩-⟨\\frac{3}{2},\\,1,\\,3⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-\\frac{3}{2},\\,1,\\,3⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14057355/example-3020.json" "file_sha256" "203f27b71cbdb193ed73d4978a08ef8e94342401b0256735cf0a638d2578da86" "basis" 1850 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14057355/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "e-3021" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find $\\displaystyle {\\int_0^1 }  \\mathbf c \\times \\mathbf f(t)  \\, \\textrm d t$ \ngiven that \n$\\displaystyle\\int_0^1\\mathbf f(t)\\,\\textrm d t = \\mathbf i-3\\,\\mathbf j-4\\,\\mathbf k$ \nand \n$\\mathbf c=\\mathbf j-\\mathbf k .$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14057355/example-3021.json" "file_sha256" "c03273a86020ea3e0bd108a41c3391276aa81a13a9aeed0d709722553282641e" "basis" 1850 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14057355/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "e-3021" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The cross-product rule states that\n\n$$\n{\\int_0^1 } \\mathbf c \\times \\mathbf f(t) \\, \\textrm d t =  \\mathbf c \\times {\\int_0^1 } \\mathbf f(t) \\, \\textrm d t  .\n$$\n\n \n\nApplying the cross-product rule, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{1}c\\times f(t)\\,\\text{d}t & =c\\times {\\int }_{0}^{1}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =(j-k)\\times (i-3\\,j-4\\,k) \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 1 & -3 & -4\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ -3 & -4\\end{aligned}|i-|\\begin{aligned}0 & -1 \\\\ 1 & -4\\end{aligned}|j+|\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & -3\\end{aligned}|k \\\\  & =(-4-3)i-(0+1)j+(0-1)k \\\\  & =-7\\,i-\\,j-\\,k.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14057355/example-3021.json" "file_sha256" "c03273a86020ea3e0bd108a41c3391276aa81a13a9aeed0d709722553282641e" "basis" 1850 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14057355/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-129178" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Calculate \n${\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{1}{3}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t$\ngiven that\n${\\int }_{1}^{0}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t=⟨-3,\\,9,\\,6⟩.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14072669/state.json" "file_sha256" "a4f31fdcadb4b096fa582c2bec4a512ba4cbd2d533a35b292a5a4c93977583e3" "basis" 2648 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14072669/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-129178" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Let's reverse the limits of integration on the known result:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{1}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t & =-{\\int }_{1}^{0}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =-⟨-3,\\,9,\\,6⟩ \\\\  & =⟨3,\\,-9,\\,-6⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, applying the scalar multiplication rule, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{1}{3}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t & =\\frac{1}{3}{\\int }_{0}^{1}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}\\cdot ⟨3,\\,-9,\\,-6⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1,\\,-3,\\,-2⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14072669/state.json" "file_sha256" "a4f31fdcadb4b096fa582c2bec4a512ba4cbd2d533a35b292a5a4c93977583e3" "basis" 2648 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14072669/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-129178" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14072669/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "be742f513a141cf803ea569247221f898bdc03e6301fb9cba23ca22ad4c28ba0" "basis" 2648 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14072